# Lore drafts (canon: soft), distilled from the existing events in phase 1.
# Curate: review, correct, then move entries to lore/hard/ with canon: hard (design §3.6).
# The Hollow Star and the founders' seal.

@lore hollow_star
keys: Hollow Star, star, light-eating star, the thing under the lake
canon: soft
text: A star that is not a light but an absence: it eats light. It sleeps beneath the Mirror Lake, behind a round door. It is not asleep so much as waiting, and it learns the names of those who look for it.

@lore founders_seal
keys: founders, seal, seven locks, seven towers
canon: soft
text: The founders built Lumenhold as a seal over the Hollow Star: seven towers, one lock in each, and a key shaped like a star that holds no light. The seal weakens over generations and must be renewed.

@lore star_key
keys: star key, key, seventh tower
canon: soft
text: The key to the founders' seal is shaped like a star and black as a hole in the world. It was kept in a star-shaped hollow at the top of the seventh tower, behind wards that shriek.

@lore seventh_tower
keys: seventh tower, locked stair
canon: soft
text: One of the seven towers has been locked for a century. At its top is a single room of dust and moonlight. When the star key is lifted, every candle in the academy goes out at once.

@lore round_door
keys: door, round door, beneath the lake, tunnel
canon: soft
text: A tunnel from the boathouse runs down to a round door at the bottom of the lake. On the night the seal weakens, it stands open a crack, and the Star looks through.

@lore drowned_bell
keys: drowned bell, bell, lake bell
canon: soft
text: A bell lies under the Mirror Lake. It tolls when the Star stirs, and once on the night the lake freezes. Edmund's silver wand hums the same note.

@lore lake_freezes
keys: frozen lake, the Night, Blossom moon, freeze
canon: soft
text: When the seal is at its weakest, on the night of the Blossom moon, the lake freezes in a single breath in the middle of spring. Cracks glow beneath the ice and things made of frost and whispers come ashore.

@lore founders_ledger
keys: Founders' Ledger, ledger, archive vault
canon: soft
text: The Founders' Ledger in the archive vault is three hundred years old. The entry for the founding year was cut out with a razor, but the impression of the pen remains on the page beneath. A client of Grisk's once paid to have another page removed.

@lore codex_hollow_names
keys: Codex of Hollow Names, codex, Restricted Section
canon: soft
text: A book in the Restricted Section that finds its readers. Its first page is a list of names; the last is still being written. Reading it turns the fingertips grey.

@lore star_mark
keys: star mark, mark, cold coin
canon: soft
text: Relics of the Star burn so cold they feel hot and can leave a pale star-shaped mark on the palm. The mark hums near the lake and makes spells come easier, which should worry its bearer more than it does.

@lore hollow_dreams
keys: dreams, black star dream
canon: soft
text: Those the Star notices dream of the lake from underneath and wake with frost on their pillows. Lavender doesn't stop the dreams, but it makes them smell nicer.

@lore man_in_grey
keys: man in grey, grey coat
canon: soft
text: A tall, polite man in a grey coat who serves the Star on behalf of the Northern families. Fountains freeze when he talks. He offers power to those who ask questions, and he has come for both Dumont children.

@lore hollow_cult
keys: Hollow cult, cult, Northern families
canon: soft
text: Northern families who serve the Star beneath the lake and send their children south to open its door. Their letters carry a black-star seal.

@lore dumont_family
keys: Dumont, Dumonts, Kael, Ilse
canon: soft
text: The Dumonts are the foremost of the Hollow families. They sent Kael to open the door; when he refused, they raised his younger sister Ilse to do it instead. Their mother has never told either child she was proud.

@lore wardens
keys: Wardens, ward-ring, headmistress
canon: soft
text: The headmistress keeps a quiet circle sworn to the founders' seal. When the seal grows thin she recruits students she trusts and gives them silver ward-rings.

@lore edmund
keys: Edmund, silver wand, frozen spring
canon: soft
text: Sixty years ago, the spring the lake froze, Maud and two friends went down to the boathouse. Edmund was the one who didn't come back. His slender silver wand was meant to go beneath the lake again, with someone who means to close the door.

@lore starcalling
keys: Starcalling, named star, starlight
canon: soft
text: An old discipline of calling down the light of a named star. Light that the Hollow Star cannot swallow is one of the few weapons the founders left.

@lore lumen_and_hollow
keys: Lumen, Hollow, light and dark, alignment
canon: soft
text: Lumenhold talks about people the way it talks about candles: some give light (Lumen), some swallow it (the Hollow). It is not a house or a club, only what people notice. Those who lean toward the Hollow find the Star noticing them back; the way out of it is slow, and usually starts with someone handing you something to do.

@lore star_herald
keys: herald, Herald of the Hollow Star, freed
canon: soft
text: If the round door is opened by one the Star already counts as its own, it goes free instead of swallowing them, and remembers who let it out. The Northern families call such a person its herald.
